# gitleaks per-finding overrides (CI escape hatch #2).
#
# When the security/privacy scan flags something that is genuinely safe and
# an inline `gitleaks:allow` comment would be too ugly (e.g. in prose), add
# the finding's FINGERPRINT here — one per line. The fingerprint is printed
# in the CI job log / step summary for every finding, in the form:
#
#   <commit-sha>:<file-path>:<rule-id>:<line-number>
#
# Prefer, in order:
#   1. Redact the value (it's usually just not needed).
#   2. Inline `# gitleaks:allow` on the flagged line (self-documenting).
#   3. A fingerprint here (for prose/YAML where a comment doesn't fit).
#   4. A rule/path allowlist in .gitleaks.toml (for whole CLASSES of
#      false positives, not individual findings).
#
# Never delete the workflow or a whole rule to silence one finding.

